WEBVTT

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:11.467
The real test is one hundred terrains the champion has never seen.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.699
Its average is 173.

00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:18.215
Half of its runs score between 163 and 207.

00:00:18.815 --> 00:00:22.775
But it falls in 9 of the one hundred, and each fall costs a lot.

00:00:22.775 --> 00:00:26.901
Almost all falls look the same: 93 percent are forward pitch-overs.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:32.952
The walker speeds up, its body rises, and then it tips onto its nose within about a third of a second.

00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:38.727
Compared with the champion from before the fall penalty, falls went from 17 to 12 in one hundred.

00:00:38.727 --> 00:00:42.963
On the same one hundred terrains, the difference is within the noise.

00:00:42.963 --> 00:00:46.178
Falling is still what pulls the average down.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:57.192
For comparison, gradient based methods on the same laptop reached about two hundred and seventy with PPO, and just over three hundred with TD3.

00:00:57.192 --> 00:01:02.595
NEAT is 99 points behind PPO, without computing a single gradient.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:09.235
All of this ran on a four core laptop with no graphics card, in 12 hours of training.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:15.511
Every network is evaluated on its own, so evolution spreads easily across the cores.
